{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ee7e39d99b57bc5adf", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Current Electricity - Test 7", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f94"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f20", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d88", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given circuit, the current in resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is:</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F19ecc83f-4cdd-4156-bded-13549af09d33.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 236px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "6886d8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d89"}, {"id": "e826ca", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d8a"}, {"id": "962d04", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d8b"}, {"id": "1f6fce", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d8c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d8d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "<p>The equivalent resistance of the circuit shown below between points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F74b8b29b-b5ea-4fc8-8a88-2433ea68bb71.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 303px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b2762d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d8e"}, {"id": "8b4510", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d8f"}, {"id": "c9f133", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d90"}, {"id": "91c3eb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d91"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d92", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "A current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>mA</mi></math> was passed through an unknown resistor which dissipated a power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Dissipated power when an ideal power supply of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is connected across it is:"}, "options": [{"id": "a87791", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d93"}, {"id": "271006", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d94"}, {"id": "5eeb57", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d95"}, {"id": "5300d6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d96"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d97", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52aa"], "question": {"text": "<p>Five equal resistances are connected in a network as shown in figure. The net resistance between the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe2eac899-646b-4371-80b7-a0cfc6807514-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 194px; height: 179px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c9b223", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d98"}, {"id": "e446a7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d99"}, {"id": "6bd0a8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d9a"}, {"id": "b8ca98", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d9b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d9c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a738"], "question": {"text": "A teacher in his physics laboratory allotted an experiment to determine the resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>G</mi></mfenced></math> a galvanometer. Students took the observations for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> deflection in the galvanometer. Which of the below is true for measuring value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math>?"}, "options": [{"id": "adea77", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> deflection method cannot be used for determining the resistance of the galvanometer.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d9d"}, {"id": "ea5cae", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;deflection method can be used and in this case the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> equals to twice the value of shunt resistance(s).", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d9e"}, {"id": "96fdbc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> deflection method can be used and in this case, the G equals to three times the value of shunt resistance(s).", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9d9f"}, {"id": "8f64d0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> deflection method can be used and in this case the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> value equals to the shunt resistance(s)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b19"], "question": {"text": "A uniform metallic wire has a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and is bent into an equilateral triangle. Then, the resistance between any two vertices of the triangle is:"}, "options": [{"id": "ee755c", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da2"}, {"id": "6d3a84", "text": "<math><mn>12</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da3"}, {"id": "be78c8", "text": "<math><mn>8</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da4"}, {"id": "49bc15", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c6855"], "question": {"text": "A galvanmeter has a coil of resistance $200 \\Omega$ with a full scale deflection at $20 \\mu \\mathrm{A}$. The value of resistance to be added to use it as an ammeter of range $(0-20) \\mathrm{mA}$ is ;"}, "options": [{"id": "5582e4", "text": "$0.40 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da7"}, {"id": "42d423", "text": "$0.20 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da8"}, {"id": "fa2a95", "text": "$0.50 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9da9"}, {"id": "7bb820", "text": "$0.10 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9daa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dab", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I :</strong> The equivalent resistance of resistors in a series combination is smaller than least resistance used in the combination.</p><p><strong>Statement II :</strong> The resistivity of the material is independent of temperature. In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b8f95a", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dac"}, {"id": "57e815", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dad"}, {"id": "28395f", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dae"}, {"id": "1b65a6", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is false but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9daf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "Two identical heater filaments are connected first in parallel and then in series. At the same applied voltage, the ratio of heat produced in same time for parallel to series will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "4481c0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db1"}, {"id": "ef4fa7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db2"}, {"id": "30bc2b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db3"}, {"id": "f1b492", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52aa"], "question": {"text": "Wheatstone bridge principle is used to measure the specific resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced></math> of given wire, having length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>, radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is the resistance of wire, then specific resistance is : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>. If the length of the wire gets doubled then the value of specific resistance will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "ada500", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db6"}, {"id": "1deadd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db7"}, {"id": "33fc61", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db8"}, {"id": "add564", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9db9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dba", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["6162fb276ed13040ec84ba05"], "question": {"text": "A galvanometer having a resistance of $20 \\Omega$ and 30 division on both sides has figure of merit 0.005 ampere/ division. The resistance that should be connected in series such that it can be used as a voltmeter upto 15 volt, is:"}, "options": [{"id": "be9050", "text": "$100 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dbb"}, {"id": "47acec", "text": "$120 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dbc"}, {"id": "ddfb31", "text": "$80 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dbd"}, {"id": "4525a5", "text": "$125 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dbe"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dbf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "In the given circuit diagram, a wire is joining points B and D. The current in this wire is:<br /><br><br /><br><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F09ee1f61-358d-41eb-bc3b-0d1e5380cee5.jpeg?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "9f2dfd", "text": "<math><mn>0.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dc0"}, {"id": "b94b07", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dc1"}, {"id": "30376a", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dc2"}, {"id": "6d7388", "text": "zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dc3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dc4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "<p>A Copper <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Cu</mi><mo>)</mo></math> rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and cross-sectional area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is joined with a similar Aluminium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Al</mi><mo>)</mo></math> rod as shown in figure. Find the resistance of the combination between the ends&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(Take resistivity of Copper <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;m</mi></math>, Resistivity of aluminium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;m</mi></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F6f7f9613-43e4-4774-ab50-3c506a7b92da-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 325px; height: 127px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "eba6af", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><m