tions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FOmPEbB895N08rB0sbcyO1qYTCuAuPJ3bOnqe1Y7kPaU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "d2b97d", "text": "$3 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dcf"}, {"id": "fa70a2", "text": "$42 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd0"}, {"id": "2cabfa", "text": "$9 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd1"}, {"id": "89359a", "text": "$6 \\Omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a738"], "question": {"text": "Consider a galvanometer shunted with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of current passes through it. What is the resistance of the given galvanometer?"}, "options": [{"id": "017db0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>245</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd4"}, {"id": "644680", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>344</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd5"}, {"id": "c7dc3d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd6"}, {"id": "4bd5b3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>226</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "What will be the most suitable combination of three resistors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> so that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is equivalent resistance of combination?"}, "options": [{"id": "66cb9f", "text": "Parallel combination of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> connected in series with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dd9"}, {"id": "61a26a", "text": "Parallel combination of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> connected in series with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dda"}, {"id": "0b7810", "text": "Series combination of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> connected in parallel with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9ddb"}, {"id": "9417b1", "text": "Series combination of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> connected in parallel with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9ddc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9ddd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements :<br /><strong>Statement I :</strong> A uniform wire of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;is cut into four equal parts. These parts are now connected in parallel. The equivalent resistance of the combination will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><strong>Statement II :</strong> Two resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></math> are connected in parallel in an electric circuit. The value of thermal energy developed in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math> will be in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9b77e2", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dde"}, {"id": "de972b", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9ddf"}, {"id": "4ed273", "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de0"}, {"id": "7bd864", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "A cell of internal resistance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> drives current through an external resistance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The power delivered by the cell to the external resistance will be maximum when:"}, "options": [{"id": "4f83b5", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de3"}, {"id": "ef26db", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de4"}, {"id": "715a4b", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de5"}, {"id": "90a867", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["6162fb276ed13040ec84ba05"], "question": {"text": "A moving coil galvanometer has resistance <math><mn>50</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and it indicates full deflection at <math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> current. A voltmeter is made using this galvanometer and a <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance. The maximum voltage, that can be measured using this voltmeter, will be close to:"}, "options": [{"id": "ea9fa9", "text": "<math><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de8"}, {"id": "655a57", "text": "<math><mn>15</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9de9"}, {"id": "e11962", "text": "<math><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9dea"}, {"id": "2a2be8", "text": "<math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9deb"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:34.553Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:34.553Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f92"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f90", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f5e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "The voltage drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance in the given figure will be _______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7024d48b-6e1a-4a85-a5e9-0851e4303b43-704ac397-2e22-460d-86ff-65d30396c129-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 204px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "850f62", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f5f"}, {"id": "9791be", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f60"}, {"id": "f64e74", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f61"}, {"id": "984b15", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f62"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f63", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "Eight copper wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> and diameter d are joined in parallel to form a single composite conductor of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. If a single copper wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></math> have the same resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>R</mi></mfenced></math> then its diameter will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "a9f1ef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f64"}, {"id": "cc96ea", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f65"}, {"id": "00bd00", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f66"}, {"id": "889f90", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f67"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f68", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f36"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eacab"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the circuit diagram shown in figure given below, the current flowing through resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ________.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F36b746a5-d3e6-4802-8a59-c2928a66370c.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 305px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2bb689", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f69"}, {"id": "ca97ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f6a"}, {"id": "102b33", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f6b"}, {"id": "6f6e3b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f6c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f6d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b9"], "question": {"text": "In the given figure an ammeter A consists of a $240 \\Omega$ coil connected in parallel to a $10 \\Omega$ shunt. The reading of the ammeter is $\\qquad$ $\\mathrm{mA}$\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FISMiXScIwIpa44YS8xetC7xdLYBvLiZYt09wd_iaGYU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "b17f35", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f6e"}, {"id": "0a0c1d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f125dcf815cd79b9f6f"}, {"id": "ca0618", "text": "", "isCorrect": nu